-- Netie gate wiring: Credentials are issued by OpenVault. The router holds no key of its own.
+- Custody: FreeRoute Core holds no key of its own. `internal/config/openvault.go`
+  adds a `credential_source` block (`openvault_url`, `seat`) and the loader fills
+  the credential pool from `GET {openvault_url}/api/freeroute/credentials` at
+  start-up, matching entries to `credentials:` by name. A config file that
+  carries `api_key`, `credentials_file` or `credentials_json`, literal or via
+  `os.environ/`, is refused by `config.Load` with the credential named. A
+  credential with no secret and no source, an unreachable or refusing OpenVault,
+  or a credential OpenVault issued nothing for, all stop the router.
+- Dev override: `NETIE_DEV_ALLOW_INLINE_KEYS=1` (exact value) accepts inline
+  keys and logs every one at WARN. It exists because the upstream config tests
+  write inline keys by design; `internal/config/netie_testmain_test.go` sets it
+  for that package and the gate tests clear it per case.
+- Default config and examples carry no provider key: `config.yaml.example`,
+  `docs/getting-started/configuration.md`, `docker-compose.yml`,
+  `docker-compose.chain.yml` and `examples/chain_mock/` (its nginx mock now also
+  stands in for the credential source at `/api/freeroute/credentials`).
+- Names: binary `freeroute-core` (Makefile, Dockerfile, README), Docker image
+  `freeroute-core`, compose service `freeroute-core`, start-up log line, the
+  `-config` flag help, the `type: air` migration error and one start-up warning.
+  The example OTEL `service_name` is `freeroute-core`.
+- Gate tests: `internal/config/netie_gate_test.go` (8 cases on the shipped
+  example and the real loader) and `internal/proxy/netie_gate_test.go` (2 cases:
+  the upstream sees only OpenVault-issued keys under round-robin; fail2ban and
+  same-type retry work on issued credentials).
+
+## Not done yet (stage 3)
+
+- Go module path `github.com/mixaill76/auto_ai_router`, Prometheus metric
+  names `auto_ai_router_*`, the Kafka `client_id` and OTEL `service_name`
+  code defaults, the otelhttp handler name and the release workflow's artifact
+  name are unchanged: each is a wire or dashboard contract and needs a build
+  plus consumer migration to rename.
+- The upstream logo (`docs/logo.svg`, referenced by README) is still upstream's.
+- `server.master_key` stays in the config file: it is the router's own
+  client-facing secret, not a provider key. Issuing it from OpenVault too is open.
+- The OpenVault issue endpoint (`/api/freeroute/credentials`, bearer seat, JSON
+  list) is the minimal interface this fork needs. It is defined here and in
