+## Credential source (OpenVault)
+
+FreeRoute Core holds no key of its own. The config file carries routing policy (names,
+types, base URLs, limits, weights, priorities) and OpenVault issues the secrets:
+
+```yaml
+credential_source:
+  openvault_url: "os.environ/NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL"  # e.g. http://127.0.0.1:5000
+  seat: "os.environ/NETIE_OPENVAULT_SEAT"          # optional: this router's issued ov_ identity
+```
+
+| Field           | Type   | Description                                                                                                   |
+| --------------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `openvault_url` | string | Base URL of the OpenVault that issues this router's provider credentials. `NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL` alone also works |
+| `seat`          | string | Optional. The router's own `ov_` identity, sent as `Authorization: Bearer`. It is not a provider key            |
+
+At start-up the loader calls `GET {openvault_url}/api/freeroute/credentials` and expects
+`{"credentials": [{"name": "...", "api_key": "...", "credentials_json": "..."}]}`. Entries are
+matched to `credentials:` by `name`. The router refuses to start, with the credential named in
+the error, when:
+
+- a credential carries `api_key`, `credentials_file` or `credentials_json` in the config file,
+  literal or via `os.environ/`;
+- a credential that needs a secret has none and no credential source is configured;
+- OpenVault is unreachable, answers anything but HTTP 200, or issues no secret for a credential.
+
+`proxy`, `air` and `vllm` credentials may run without a secret, as upstream allows.
+
+Local development only: `NETIE_DEV_ALLOW_INLINE_KEYS=1` lets a file carry inline keys. Every
+accepted key is logged at WARN with the credential name. Never set it in production.
+
 ## Credentials
 
 Each credential defines a connection to an LLM provider. See [Providers](../providers/index.md) for details on each type.
+Secrets are never written here: see [Credential source (OpenVault)](#credential-source-openvault).
 
